{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>A man's garment upon a woman</b> — in gematria: כלי תורה, alluding that a person should not teach his daughter Torah." "<b>Upon a woman</b> — twice: כלי גבר על אשה. If my heart was enticed upon a woman — this is what they said, that it speaks of a woman who dons a man's garment in order to disguise herself and commit harlotry, as written: אם נפתה לבי על אשה ועל פתח רעי ארבתי." "<b>For it is an abomination to HaShem</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {1 "The phrase אם נפתה לבי על אשה ועל פתח רעי ארבתי is quoted from Job 31:9, which Ba'al HaTurim reads as a second scriptural occurrence of על אשה alongside the present verse."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:17.710254692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}